{
  "about": "Hindi glossary for drharshmaheshwari.com. Every Hindi translation must use these terms: tests/i18n.test.mjs checks that when an English text contains a term, its Hindi has one of the accepted forms (nukta and chandrabindu are ignored when comparing). Change a term here, then retranslate what uses it. docs/translation.md has the rules.",
  "register": "Everyday spoken Hindi (Hindustani) that a family in Lucknow, Raipur or Delhi would use, not textbook Sanskritised Hindi. Common English health words that people say in Hindi stay as they are said (BMI, ब्लड शुगर, डायबिटीज़). Short sentences. Numbers in 0-9, never Devanagari digits. Units as in English (cm, kg).",
